        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "01ec7a44-447c-5811-8d71-590ea88fe449",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Friedrich von Schiller, Jules Massenet, Henri Caïn, Loretta Di Franco\n- Works: Luisa Miller, Don Quichotte, Kabale und Liebe, Lucia di Lammermoor\n- Organizations: Metropolitan Opera\n- Topics: Opera roles and librettos\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich von Schiller wrote the play \"Kabale und Liebe\" (\"Intrigue and Love\").\n- Giuseppe Verdi composed \"Luisa Miller,\" a three-act opera with an Italian libretto by Salvadore Cammarano based on Friedrich von Schiller's play \"Kabale und Liebe.\"\n- Jules Massenet composed \"Don Quichotte\" (\"Don Quixote\"), a five-act opera with a French libretto by Henri Caïn.\n- Loretta Di Franco performed many roles at the Metropolitan Opera, including Laura in \"Luisa Miller\" and the title role in \"Lucia di Lammermoor.\"\n- Loretta Di Franco also performed roles at the Metropolitan Opera in operas including \"La traviata,\" \"Jenůfa,\" \"The Marriage of Figaro,\" \"Rigoletto,\" \"Hansel and Gretel,\" \"The Magic Flute,\" \"Carmen,\" \"Die Walküre,\" \"Madama Butterfly,\" \"La bohème,\" \"Un ballo in maschera,\" \"Boris Godunov,\" and \"Don Giovanni.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "efb356d7-6092-5031-9814-be63922d74e7",
        "text": "Page: Luisa Miller. Sentence: Luisa Miller is an opera in three acts by Giuseppe Verdi to an Italian libretto by Salvadore Cammarano, based on the play \"Kabale und Liebe\" (\"Intrigue and Love\") by the German dramatist Friedrich von Schiller.\nPage: Don Quichotte. Sentence: Don Quichotte (\"Don Quixote\") is an opera in five acts by Jules Massenet to a French libretto by Henri Caïn.\nPage: Loretta Di Franco. Sentence: Some of the parts she performed at the Met included Annina in \"La traviata\", both the Aunt and Barena in Janáček's \"Jenůfa\", Barbarina and Marcellina in \"The Marriage of Figaro\", Berta in \"The Barber of Seville\", Countess Ceprano in \"Rigoletto\", the Dew Fairy and the Sandman in \"Hansel and Gretel\", Feklusa in \"Káťa Kabanová\", the First Lady in \"The Magic Flute\", the Flower Seller in Britten's \"Death in Venice\", Frasquita in \"Carmen\", Gerhilde in \"Die Walküre\", Giannetta in \"L'elisir d'amore\", Helen in \"Mourning Becomes Electra\", Ines in \"Il trovatore\", Jouvenot in \"Adriana Lecouvreur\", Kate Pinkerton in \"Madama Butterfly\", Laura in \"Luisa Miller\", Lauretta in \"Gianni Schichi\", Lisa in \"La sonnambula\", Marianne in \"Der Rosenkavalier\", Marthe in \"Faust\", Musetta in \"La bohème\", Oscar in \"Un ballo in maschera\", Samaritana in \"Francesca da Rimini\", Woglinde in both \"Das Rheingold\" and \"Götterdämmerung\", Xenia in \"Boris Godunov\", Zerlina in \"Don Giovanni\", and title role in \"Lucia di Lammermoor\".",
